# {{name}}

A LocalReel storage plugin generated by `localreel-plugin-cli new` ({{language}}).

- `manifest.json` declares the plugin (id `{{id}}`, api `localreel.plugin/v1`,
  entry `{{script}}` run by `{{runtime}}`).
- `{{script}}` implements the sidecar protocol: it binds loopback, prints one
  `ready` line, checks `X-LocalReel-Token`, and serves `stat`/`list`/`walk`/`read`.
- `build.ps1` (Windows) or `build.sh` (Unix) stages `pkg/manifest.json` and the
  script; there is no compilation step.

## Build and pack

```sh
./build.sh                       # Windows: .\build.ps1
localreel-plugin-cli pack pkg --out dist/{{id}}.lrplug
localreel-plugin-cli inspect dist/{{id}}.lrplug
```

The host needs the `{{runtime}}` interpreter on `PATH`.

## Install

```toml
[[plugins]]
package = "dist/{{id}}.lrplug"

[plugins.config]
root = "D:/media"
```
